":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T08:04:41-07:00","id":1125598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125434-golden-age-of-science-fiction-de2?p=1125478#post1125478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross posted from the regular DE2 thread, but musing over historical events...<br /> <br /> ...while this stuff isn't *directly* related to sci-fi fiction written or conceived of at the time, it does relate to the type of thing you would find in sci-fi stories.<br /> <br /> Within the time period there's the Battle of Los Angeles of 1942. Where in the middle of the night anti-aircraft gun emplacements in LA fired into the night at supposed enemy aircraft. Where afterwards the military brushed if off saying that the soldiers were actually firing upon was a mundane weather balloon and that it was a mistake made by some tense, overexcited airsmen. Ufologists and conspiracy theorists, however, claim that the LA military were actually engaged with extraterrestrial aircraft, and the military and government were trying to cover it up.<br /> <br /> There's also the Roswell incident that also featured a flying object initially described as a &amp;quot;flying disc&amp;quot; and that the military later claimed that it was just a weather balloon but that Ufologists and conspiracy theorist also claim was an alien craft, but that happened in 1947, a year after the announced timeframe of this Era. So...eh.</div> </div> </div> </div> I remember hearing about the Battle of LA in one of those UFO concpiracy shows on Netflix! Weird era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:26:14-07:00","id":1125631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125434-golden-age-of-science-fiction-de2?p=1125573#post1125573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likely not, that doesn't happen until 1955, but I'd be shocked if Hubbard himself wasn't meantioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus they tend to be perfectly fine slinging lawsuits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T18:08:17-07:00","id":1125746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125434-golden-age-of-science-fiction-de2?p=1125631#post1125631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus they tend to be perfectly fine slinging lawsuits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that. <br /> <br /> Which is a pity, because regardless of my personal thoughts about the way Scientology conducts itself (and some of its more... escentric personalities) their tenets are facinating, especially how they blend the occult with science fiction. Seeing an interpretation of them in CofD would be pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T18:15:07-07:00","id":1125748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125434-golden-age-of-science-fiction-de2?p=1125746#post1125746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a pity, because regardless of my personal thoughts about the way Scientology conducts itself (and some of its more... escentric personalities) their tenets are facinating, especially how they blend the occult with science fiction. Seeing an interpretation of them in CofD would be pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check the Banishers book.<br /> <br /> 'In the mid-1950s, the minor pulp science fiction author Levi Bones founded a fringe religion, which he termed &quot;Panography.\u201d His motives were a mystery. At least one source says he founded the faith on a bet; others point to the founder\u2019s unpublished writings on philosophy and religion, or his association with fringe occult groups such as Aleister Crowley\u2019s Ordo Templi Orientis. (Crowley characterized Bones as a lout and confidence man.) In any event, Bones released an amphetamine-fueled pseudoscientific history of the universe that, in conjunction with an equally dodgy book on mental health he\u2019d written a year earlier, set down the tenets of the faith.'<br /> <br /> It became the Militant Auditors Division.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:41:05-07:00","id":1126957,"title":"","content":"I'm a little lost on this one. Is it a pulp-y 1940s High Weirdness setting, or a look at how an emergent literary movement has impacted the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:50:34-07:00","id":1126962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125434-golden-age-of-science-fiction-de2?p=1126957#post1126957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little lost on this one. Is it a pulp-y 1940s High Weirdness setting, or a look at how an emergent literary movement has impacted the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming a mix that favours the latter. At least, that's the way I'd write it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sp